!!! Row census — node


This table covers every `buildTable()` row in `packages/lararium-node/src/vault-carriers.ts:236-398`. “Current” names the code's custody class. “Owner / target” is the K15 contract. Where the source only names a filename, ''LEAD'' requires a payload and caller audit before the classification can be implemented. There is no implicit S catchall.

| Current row and code line | Current | Owner / target and required cut |
| `vessel-key` `:240-242` | floor | ''S, OPEN JOINT:'' private place signing seed owned by this node. Its public verifying key belongs in F. The signer options appear below; it is never a custody VK or face ancestor. `node-vessel-identity.ts:429-442,451-487` proves the private seed is read from disk and used at the floor door. |
| `vessel-kel` `:243-245` | floor | ''F:'' public inception/signature, node place principal. |
| `s-slots` `:246-248` | floor | ''D/S split:'' retire the omnibus VK tree. Each face gets its own FCK tree; a node S tree exists only for named S rows. No face FCK wrapper under a node key. |
| `sk-slots` `:249-251` | floor | ''S conditional, node:'' retire current VK-to-SK wrapping. No serving row exists today (`:12-14`). A future serving payload gets its own named S key and boot rule before this tree survives. |
| `fk-slots` `face-custody.ts` | floor | ''D (the face's own tree):'' one tree per face at `faces/<fcid>/fk-slots.bin`, wrapping that face's random custody key under each human route that face asked for. No VK wraps it and no sibling face's route opens it; the face's rows and this tree rest in one directory, so a bundle or a removal moves them together. |
| `face-index` `face-index.ts` | floor-plain | ''F:'' the one floor row that names the faces a node can unlock before any face opens: the count of faces (tombstones included), each group's digest, each founding ask's digest and each random directory name, and no other byte. It routes and never decides; see #/the-floor-index. |
| `vessel-card` `:254-256` | floor-plain | ''F:'' public node contact card. |
| `charter` `:257-259` | floor-plain | ''F:'' signed public founding charter. |
