| `keyhive-archive` `:290-291` | hot | ''D:'' split the vessel archive into one identity/archive per PersonaGroup, with no identity above them (`stable-founding-road.mem:203,459`). Node archive row selection is an OPEN JOINT below. |
| `veil-archive` `:292-293` | face-hot | ''D:'' the node rests each face's archive at `veil-archive-g<digest of its PersonaGroup>`, so no free index selects it; its FCK arrives with the K15.6 fence. |
| `face-atom` `face-atom-store.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' the face's random atom seed, one per (vessel, PersonaGroup), the device edge's delegate and countersigner and the face's Keyhive Individual. The row's file name carries the SHA-256 digest of its PersonaGroup, so no clear file names a face, and the face-atom custody contract of `@lararium/mesh` (`face-atom-custody.ts`) holds stand, read and keep: absent mints, the same bytes read as a no-op, other bytes refuse as `FaceAtomConflict`. It rests under the vessel key until the K15.6 fence moves it under that face's FCK; it never rides a bundle, a wire or a board. |
